<title>USA: ValuJet Oct load factor rises to 72.1 pct.</title>
<headline>ValuJet Oct load factor rises to 72.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>October</p>
<p>						 1996		  1995</p>
<p> Load factor - percent     72.1		64.2</p>
<p> Revenue passenger miles   70,452	    241,472</p>
<p> Available seat miles	97,659	    376,260</p>
<p> Enplaned passengers	 154,292	   478,361</p>
<p>					    Year-to-date</p>
<p> Load factor - percent     57.6		70.0</p>
<p> Revenue passenger miles   1,383,500	 2,093,095</p>
<p> Available seat miles	2,400,437	 2,991,272</p>
<p> Enplaned Passengers	 2,678,020	 4,150,722</p>
<p>(Revenue passenger and available seat miles in 000,000s)</p>
<p>Full company name is ValuJet Inc.</p>
<p>NOTES: Year-to-date operations 1996 figures represent flight operations from January 1 to June 17, 1996, September 30, 1996 and the month of October. ValuJet had 15 aircraft during October 1996 compared to 36 aircraft in October 1995. The carrier was grounded from mid-June to September 29, for safety concerns after its Flight 592 crashed, killing all 110 people on board.  -- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
